 "notes": "Fig. 5 of Kohri & Kodama (arXiv:1704.05189): 95% C.L. contour in the (m_a, g_agamma) plane from chi^2 fits combining H2356-309 and 1ES1101-232 TeV gamma-ray spectra. This is a PREFERRED/ALLOWED region (a hint), not an exclusion: inside the contour photon-ALP mixing resolves the tension between CIBER-level cosmic IR background and TeV transparency. Scenario reported: the outer 'CIBER only' (CIBER + Franceschini-Th) contour, i.e. the paper's headline region quoted in the abstract (m_a ~ 7e-10 - 5e-8 eV, g ~ 1.5e-11 GeV^-1 lower edge; contour agrees: g_min=1.52e-11, m_min=6.7e-10). The inner CIBER+IRTS+AKARI contour was not used. Points trace the closed contour boundary as an ordered loop (not monotonic in mass): starting where the left arm exits the frame top (m~3.4e-9 eV, g=1e-9 GeV^-1), down the left side, along the bottom, up the right side and out the frame top at m~2.6e-7 eV; couplings clipped at the plot top g=1e-9 GeV^-1 (region is open above). Extracted from the vector EPS (magagComb.eps) rendered at 288 dpi with axis calibration taken from the vector frame coordinates (log-log axes: 1e-10..1e-6 eV, 1e-12..1e-9 GeV^-1); dashed-stroke gaps bridged by morphological closing, centerline by skeletonization. No dark-matter density assumption (astrophysical transparency argument), so no rescaling.",
